 <section id="adaptive-driver-contracts-20260928"><h2>Isolated adaptive driver contracts</h2><p>BUG-058 experimental complete build only. Existing interface profiles below supply conservative registers and memory rules; entry-specific ownership is described in the canonical ticket.</p><ul><li id="routine-resident-runtime-ad-clock-exec"><code>AD_CLOCK_EXEC</code>: Read an atomic raw VBlank snapshot through the fitted mapped gateway. Profile: <a href="#profile-root">root</a>.</li><li id="routine-resident-runtime-ad-reset-exec"><code>AD_RESET_EXEC</code>: Rebase adaptive phase time and clear both damage journals outside active publication. Profile: <a href="#profile-state">state</a>.</li><li id="routine-resident-runtime-ad-work-exec"><code>AD_WORK_EXEC</code>: Execute the active logical batch, damage reduction, audio service and BACK publication transaction. Profile: <a href="#profile-framebuffer">framebuffer</a>.</li><li id="routine-resident-runtime-adaptive-install-active"><code>adaptive_install_active</code>: Restore the active low-RAM driver from staged page $3D after a presentation overlay retires. Profile: <a href="#profile-copy">copy</a>.</li><li id="routine-audio-runtime-aas-clock"><code>aas_clock</code>: Read an atomic raw VBlank snapshot without changing caller IRQ state. Profile: <a href="#profile-audio">audio</a>.</li><li id="routine-audio-runtime-aas-dirty"><code>aas_dirty</code>: Detect semantic-state or queue changes before admitting audio; no note ages here. Profile: <a href="#profile-audio">audio</a>.</li><li id="routine-audio-runtime-aas-prime"><code>aas_prime</code>: Decode only newly admitted zero-wait voices; never age an existing dwell. Profile: <a href="#profile-audio">audio</a>.</li><li id="routine-audio-runtime-audio-adaptive-api"><code>audio_adaptive_api</code>: Separate elapsed-note service, semantic admission, audible publication and explicit phase rebase. Profile: <a href="#profile-audio">audio</a>.</li></ul></section>
-<section id="profile-keybindings"><h2>Session keybinding interface</h2><p><strong>inputs:</strong> Physical CoCo switch columns, session bindings, capture state and prepared menu BACK; B selects scan, paint, menu tick or reset.</p><p><strong>outputs:</strong> Held action mask, fresh credit/start/menu edges, retained bindings or selected menu pixels; menu tick returns B=$FF to retain or B=6 to return.</p><p><strong>clobbers:</strong> A, B, D, X, Y, U and condition codes except source-preserved registers; every stack return is balanced.</p><p><strong>reads:</strong> PIA keyboard rows, retired-boot-area bindings/capture state, immutable font masks and authored key-name/menu records.</p><p><strong>writes:</strong> Unbanked low RAM $0287-$029A and menu-owned edge/selection/dirty bytes; prepared BACK pixels and module-local owner selection cache.</p><p><strong>side effects:</strong> Capture suppresses global and local consumers through accepted-key release; painting calls the resident mask renderer without changing PAR5.</p><p><strong>invariants:</strong> The existing page-$3D stream owns code/data at $BA00; caller gateway restores its PAR5; bindings reset at startup and never persist to storage.</p></section><section id="routine-resident-runtime-presentation-key-service"><h3><code>presentation_key_service</code></h3><p>Call the bounded physical key component while preserving the caller bank mapping. Interface: <a href="#profile-input">input</a>. Source: <code>src/main.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-service"><h3><code>key_service</code></h3><p>Dispatch physical input, authored menu painting, capture navigation or default initialization. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-init"><h3><code>key_init</code></h3><p>Restore seven default physical bindings and clear capture and repaint history. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-scan"><h3><code>key_scan</code></h3><p>Sample eight physical columns and produce held actions and fresh consumer edges. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-down"><h3><code>key_down</code></h3><p>Test one column-times-eight-plus-row physical switch while preserving caller indexes. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-capture"><h3><code>key_capture</code></h3><p>Reject conflicting or ambiguous keys and consume accepted or cancelled capture through release. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-tick"><h3><code>key_tick</code></h3><p>Navigate the seven actions and BACK or begin waiting for a replacement switch. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-paint"><h3><code>key_paint</code></h3><p>Repaint all hydrated rows or only the previous and current selected rows for the prepared owner. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-waiting"><h3><code>key_waiting</code></h3><p>Report whether the current row owns active capture parentheses. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-name"><h3><code>key_name</code></h3><p>Resolve a physical switch to its single glyph or descriptive key name. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-text"><h3><code>key_text</code></h3><p>Paint an authored length-delimited glyph run. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-keybinding-runtime-key-char"><h3><code>key_char</code></h3><p>Paint one source glyph through the resident shared mask renderer. Interface: <a href="#profile-keybindings">keybindings</a>. Source: <code>src/keybinding_runtime.s</code>; current source-reference module pages retain emitted-address and call evidence.</p></section><section id="routine-resident-runtime-asset-draw-part-value"><h3><code>asset_draw_part_value</code></h3><p>BUG061 integrated and accepted at669b157; current fixed part formatter. Input A=part1–255 and HUD_X=hundreds column. Compute hundreds in B and remainder in A, then jump to immutable asset_part_digits; write blank for zero hundreds followed by fixed tens/units through the existing two-digit writer. Uses the last compact font glyph only under the producer blank-mask guard. Writes HUD_X and target framebuffer glyph cells; preserves stage/lives and existing MMU ownership. Clobbers A/B and follows the existing render interface. Source: src/main.s and src/shared_text_runtime.inc. Current capacity and integration qualification are recorded in <a href="../tickets/bug-061-global-two-digit-part-format.html#split-formatter-fit-20261003">BUG061</a>.</p></section><section id="routine-highscore-helper-stage-player-score"><h3><code>stage_player_score</code></h3><p>BUG-069 integrated and accepted at7f52f46; parent full build and visible score handoff verified. Existing mapped stage helper paints six score digits at x33–38,row2 in light green during hidden hydration. Context2 reads current SCORE_BCD; contexts0/1 paint zero. Existing stage_panel_char preserves loop registers; score accounting and MMU ownership remain unchanged.</p></section><section id="routine-resident-runtime-life-marker-position"><h3><code>life_marker_position</code></h3><p>Map reserve slots0–11 to authored HUD tile roots; write HUD_X and HUD_Y only. Input A is slot0–11; A/B and condition codes are scratch. HUD origin is x33+2*(slot%3), y21−2*(slot//3). No life-counter mutation or actor-transfer ownership. Interface: <a href="#profile-render">render</a>. Source: <code>src/shared_text_runtime.inc</code>, mirrored by src/main.s and the current source-reference registry. <a href="../tickets/bug-062-twelve-life-indicator-grid.html">Approved grid contract</a>.</p></section><section id="routine-enemy-runtime-player-entry-width"><h2>player_entry_width — persistent HUD transfer width</h2><p>BUG084 helper in existing src/enemy_runtime.s. Input: INITIAL_ENTRY_STATE and hydrated current/old PLAYER_FB low byte. During WALKOUT/OFFSCREEN only, return/write PLAYER_DX=min(8,max(0,160−byte-column)); other states retain eight packed bytes. A/B/condition codes are scratch; no life-counter or framebuffer-owner mutation. Horizontal HUD rows are page-aligned. The existing persistent capture/restore/commit loops retain16 rows and eight-byte stage/save-under strides while framebuffer reads/writes use the visible width. At x320, width is zero; both owner histories must retire before normal maze entry reuses full width. Excluded nonpersistent vertical-clipping path remains unchanged. <a href="../tickets/bug-084-marker-exit-direction.html">Approved transfer contract and current evidence</a>.</section><section id="routine-resident-runtime-hud-fb-address"><h2>hud_fb_address — resolve a HUD cell framebuffer address</h2><p>Existing src/main.s render helper. Read the full-width HUD_X and HUD_Y coordinates and return X=FB_VIRT+(HUD_Y*1280)+(HUD_X*4); A/B/D and condition codes are scratch. Shared by life-marker erasure, HUD tile drawing and marker-entry setup. Interface: <a href="#profile-render">render</a>.</p></section><section id="routine-resident-runtime-marker-entry-begin"><h2>marker_entry_begin — arm the already-consumed life</h2><p>Existing src/main.s entry-state helper; interface <a href="#profile-movement">movement</a>. Initial WAIT_STAGE consumes one reserve only after RF_STAGE commits; if the latest post-PSG status is busy, state1 and DEATH_TIMER=1 wait without repeating the decrement. Death replacement arrives after its existing decrement and uses the same wait sentinel only when prior music remains busy. On idle, read the already-decremented count as the consumed HUD slot, seed DEATH_TIMER=80 before HUD rendering mutates scratch, call life_marker_position and hud_fb_address, set DIR/face east and stateWALKOUT, and merge RF_LIVES|RF_PLAYER. A/B/D and condition codes are scratch. The accepted two-pixel WALKOUT/OFFSCREEN ticks count down the exit pad while both owner histories are checked every callback; state4 retains the Y18 final pose until the published music status is idle after the existing pending-render IRQ gate. The routine never decrements LIVES, resets maze/stage, or changes manual/want. Zero reserves retain the existing game-over branch. <a href="../tickets/bug-085-marker-every-life.html">Approved replacement-life contract</a>.</p></section><section id="routine-highscore-helper-logo-vbord-clock"><h2>logo_vbord_clock</h2><p>BUG081 integrated source pending combined acceptance. IRQ-atomic FRAMES sample advances the fixed31-VBL logo phase using reserved A8FD-A8FF state; preserves caller PAR4 and CC. Screen changes reinitialize phase/owner caches; actor D3 remains unchanged. Interface details and live qualification are recorded in <a href="../tickets/bug-081-logo-animation-dwell.html">BUG081</a>.</p></section></main>
+<section id="profile-keybindings"><h2>Session keybinding interface</h2><p><strong>inputs:</strong> Physical CoCo switch columns; in INPUT_JOYSTICK builds, raw 0..63 axes from conditional PRES_MAIN_JOY_AXIS on presentation screens, including name entry; session bindings, capture state and prepared menu BACK. B selects scan, paint, menu tick or reset.</p><p><strong>outputs:</strong> Five held gameplay actions, fresh fixed coin/menu edges, and a fresh automatic-loop wake token from keyboard or cardinal joystick direction; retained bindings or selected menu pixels. No joystick fire-button event is read.</p><p><strong>clobbers:</strong> A, B, D, X, Y, U and condition codes except source-preserved registers; every stack return is balanced.</p><p><strong>reads:</strong> PIA keyboard rows and, on presentation screens in joystick builds, the existing raw joystick-axis callback; retired-boot-area bindings/capture state, immutable font masks and authored key-name/menu records.</p><p><strong>writes:</strong> Unbanked low RAM $0287-$029A, profile-local joystick direction history in the page-$3D keybinding module, and menu-owned edge/selection/dirty bytes; prepared BACK pixels and module-local owner selection cache.</p><p><strong>side effects:</strong> Capture suppresses global and local consumers through accepted-key release. Joystick sampling normalizes raw axes to one cardinal dead-zone edge without writing JOY/player/name state and restores PIA2 DAC and the established audio_select_gmc PIA selectors. All non-emitting presentation screens, including name entry, refresh direction history silently; only automatic-loop owners publish changed non-neutral directions. Painting calls the resident mask renderer without changing PAR5.</p><p><strong>invariants:</strong> KB_ROWS at $028E-$0295 is exclusive raw-scan history: key_init seeds impossible $FF before scanning, and key_scan accumulates current-and-not-previous bits before each column overwrite. The joystick callback exists only